## 3. Named Range Conventions

- **Raw inputs:** `SOURCE_description_year` (e.g., `BAL_cash_marketable_securities_2024`, `INC_sales`, `CASH_operating`)
- **Du Pont cross-reference outputs:** `RATIO_asset_turnover`, `RATIO_operating_profit_margin`, `RATIO_debt_burden`, `RATIO_leverage`
- **Derived intermediates:** `startYear_`, `currentYear_`, and `avg_` prefixes

All named ranges are defined in the Excel Name Manager; no bare cell references appear in the Ratios tab.

---

## 4. Assumptions & Constraints

- Tax rate assumed at statutory 21.4%; not derived from `INC_taxes / INC_taxable_income`
- Interest expense on simple annual basis; no sub-period compounding
- No off-balance-sheet items included; operating leases and pension obligations not capitalized
- Total capitalization = long-term debt (after 1 yr) + shareholders' equity — excludes short-term debt ($4.4B) and current LTD ($6.7B)
- Quick ratio uses trade receivables only; Cat Financial finance receivables ($9.6B) excluded
- WACC of 7.9% is an analyst estimate with no formal CAPM build-up
- Share price ($349.58) reflects fiscal year-end close; market cap = `share_price × shares_outstanding`, no diluted adjustment
- Average balances = simple average of FY2023 and FY2024 period-end figures

