## 7. Model Review

### What Was Built Correctly

The named-range architecture is the model's strongest feature — every input is descriptively named, the Du Pont section cross-references `RATIO_*` ranges rather than bare cell addresses, and the Notes tab logs every formula correction with a plain-language explanation. Balance sheet checks pass for both years. Start-of-year vs. average-based profitability variants are consistently maintained.

### What to Improve

- Quick ratio excludes Cat Financial finance receivables ($9.6B) without an inline cell note — embed documentation directly
- Total capitalization omits short-term debt ($4.4B) and current LTD ($6.7B); label the metric explicitly or include all debt
- Tax rate should be derived as `INC_taxes / INC_taxable_income` rather than manually assumed at 21.4%
- WACC has no build-up; add a sensitivity table (6%–10%) to stress-test EVA for a CFO audience
- Layout: freeze panes at category headers, add conditional formatting for out-of-norm ratios, group rows by category
- Add free cash flow (`CASH_operating − CASH_capex = $12,482M`) to contextualize the $7.8B share repurchase

